 "title": "Treasurer - Madison County Courthouse Nebraska",
 "text": "Treasurer - Madison County Courthouse Nebraska\nSkip to content.\nMadison County Courthouse south entrance will be closed beginning at 7:00 A.M. on Wednesday, October 21, 2026, and will remain closed until 12:00 P.M. on Thursday, October 22, 2026.\nX\nMenu\n-->\nEmployment\nCalendar\nAbout\nContact Us\nSearch for:\nMenu\nHome\nDepartments Assessor\nClerk\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Court\nDistrict Court\nElections\nHighway Department\nPublic Defender\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeteran Services\nNoxious Weed Authority\nCounty Services Budget\nAgendas\nMeetings\nPublic Notice\nProceedings\nBoard of Commissioners\nWhere do I…? Find Election Info\nRegister to Vote\nRegister/Title A Vehicle\nObtain & Learn About Permits\nAgencies Fair Housing\nUtility Bill Assistance\nEmergency Management\nCaring Senior Resources – Emergency Housing Guide\nSenior Housing Net-Emergency Housing Guide\nVisitors Bureau\nUNL County Extension\nMadison County Fair\nMedicare Options for Nebraska Residents\nMedicare Resources for Immigrant Populations\nMedicare Resources for Immigrant Populations-Spanish\nEmployment\nCalendar\nAbout\nContact Us\nTreasurer\nWe strive to serve the public in a helpful, courteous and efficient manner, while maintaining the utmost integrity and fairness. The customers of the Madison County Treasurer’s Office are the purpose of our work.\nProperty Tax Information\nWhen are real property taxes due?\nReal property taxes are due December 31. The first half of the tax becomes delinquent on the following May 1 and the second half becomes delinquent on September 1.\nWhen are personal property taxes due?\nPersonal property taxes are due December 31. The first half of the tax becomes delinquent on the following May 1 and the second half becomes delinquent on September 1.\nOn the due date, the taxes become a first lien on all personal property you own. If the taxes are not paid, any personal property you own, whether taxable or not, is subject to seizure in order to satisfy the lien.\nHelpful Links\nBoat Registration (renewal only)\nDriver and Vehicle Records Division\nDrivers License Examining Division\nMotorboat Title Division\nNebraska Taxes On-line\nVehicle Titling Information\nDonna Primrose\nTreasurer\nOffice Hours\n8:30 A.M. to 5:00 P.M.\nPhone:\n402-454-3311\nDial option 1\nFax:\n402-454-3506\nEmail:\nSend Email\nMail:\nPO Box 270\nMadison NE, 68748-270\nLocation:\n1313 North Main Street,\nMadison NE 68748\nHours:\nMonday-Friday\n8:30 A.M. – 5:00 P.M.\nScroll To Top\nAddress\nMadison County Courthouse\n1313 North Main Street\nPO Box 290\nMadison, Nebraska 68748\nPhone: (402) 454-3311\nHours: Mon - Fri 8:00AM - 5:00PM\nHours may vary per office.\nTreasurer's Office 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM\nQuick Links:\nFAQ\nContacts\nEmployment\n©2026 Madison County Courthouse",
